Mesa's Metal WSI on Minkar, the GPU's present: when the device is the GPU
that holds CAMetalLayer's drawables (IOSurfaces in the display GPU's
VRAM), the swapchain takes the Metal path's image blit, and the copy it
records at each acquire goes from the image into the drawable's IOSurface
itself: its VRAM imported by the shared buffer's name (a dma-buf
descriptor, minkar_drm_shared_buffer_fd), or its memory in place when it
is the system's (VK_EXT_external_memory_host); imports are kept by the
surface's ID. The drawable is presented once the copy is done. No CPU
copy is left. Other devices, software drivers and MINKAR_WSI_CPU keep
patch 0005's CPU copy; MINKAR_WSI_DEBUG says which path a swapchain took.
The WSI's dispatch gets vkGetMemoryFdPropertiesKHR and
vkGetMemoryHostPointerPropertiesEXT; it links IOKit and CoreFoundation
to find the display's GPU.

